<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">elite</ansi>

An elite class is the second promotion of a route. At level 30 a character
with an advanced class may promote again, to the elite class that continues
its route. Elite classes keep every rank of the advanced class and add their
own, up to level 60. Companions promote the same way.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">class</ansi>                              shows "promote ready" or what it waits on
  <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] [class]</ansi>     preview: gate, role, the ranks you have already
                                     reached, the next one
  <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] [class] confirm</ansi>   make it

Routes are final: an elite class continues the route you took at level 10, and
there is no switching. A character must hold the advanced class first; a
level 30 character who never promoted can take both steps in one visit
(<ansi fg="command">class promote priest confirm</ansi>, then <ansi fg="command">class promote hierarch confirm</ansi>). The elite
class's ranks that your level has already reached start at once.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The gate</ansi>

A good route needs alignment +30 or higher at the moment you promote, an evil
route -30 or lower, and a neutral route nothing. If your alignment is not yet
right, <ansi fg="command">class</ansi> says the promotion is waiting; you keep your ranks and promote
when your alignment recovers (<ansi fg="command">help alignment</ansi>). The company window shows the same
as "Promotion ready" or "Promotion waiting on alignment".

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

From level 35 an elite character's talent slots (35, 45, 55) offer a second
list, the elite talents (every elite of a lineage shares one), beside the lineage's usual five. See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The elite classes</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Warrior</ansi>
  Paladin         good      Knight route: heals, auras and Smite    <ansi fg="command">help warrior-routes</ansi>
  Warlord         neutral   Mercenary route: marks foes, quickens   <ansi fg="command">help warlord</ansi>
  Dread Knight    evil      Blackguard route: Aura of Dread, Terror <ansi fg="command">help warrior-routes</ansi>
  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Cleric</ansi>
  Hierarch        good      Priest route: Call the Host             <ansi fg="command">help summoning</ansi>
  Elder Druid     neutral   Druid route: groves and healing         <ansi fg="command">help cleric-routes</ansi>
  Demonologist    evil      Blood Priest route: Bind the Fiend      <ansi fg="command">help summoning</ansi>
  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Wizard</ansi>
  Archon          good      Theurgist route: Counterspell, wards    <ansi fg="command">help archon</ansi>
  Archmage        neutral   Arcanist route: Overchannel, Storm      <ansi fg="command">help archmage</ansi>
  Necromancer     evil      Warlock route: thralls, Life Drain      <ansi fg="command">help necromancer</ansi>
  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Witch</ansi>
  Wise One        good      Hedge Witch route: Hearthward           <ansi fg="command">help wise-one</ansi>
  Coven Mother    neutral   Coven Sage route: surer, longer hexes   <ansi fg="command">help coven-mother</ansi>
  Crone of Ash    evil      Hag route: curses that spread and kill  <ansi fg="command">help crone-of-ash</ansi>

The other lineages' elite classes (Pathfinder, Swordmaster, Nightblade,
Sentinel, Marksman, Ravager, and the Samurai's Sword Saint, Shogun and Kenshi)
are still to come; until they arrive those characters keep their advanced
class's ranks.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help alignment</ansi>.
